# Riziki Industrial Chemicals — the two hostnames, for the shared edge.
#
# WHERE THIS FILE GOES: /srv/edge/sites/rizikichemicals.caddy on the server.
# It is NOT read from the repo. `edge-caddy`, the proxy that owns ports 80 and
# 443 for every site on this box, imports /srv/edge/sites/*.caddy — so a change
# here does nothing until it is copied across and the edge is reloaded. See
# DEPLOY.md, "The website and the edge".
#
# This used to be a whole Caddyfile for a Caddy of our own, binding 80 and 443
# directly. One process can hold a port; the edge already held both. So that
# proxy never started, the website had no route at all, and the bare domain
# fell through to another site on the server — while the shop system kept
# working and hid the fault. Worse: had it ever won the startup race, it knew
# three hostnames and would have taken the other fifteen sites down.
#
# The upstreams are container names on the `edge` network, which is how every
# other site file here addresses its app.

# The marketing site.
rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	reverse_proxy riziki-pos-web-1:80
}

# One canonical host: www redirects rather than serving a duplicate site.
www.rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	redir https://rizikichemicals.co.ke{uri} permanent
}

# The shop system. HTTPS is not cosmetic here: the offline mode (service
# worker) and "install to home screen" only work on a secure origin, and
# offline is the feature the counter phone depends on.
pos.rizikichemicals.co.ke {
	reverse_proxy riziki-pos-pos-1:3100
	encode zstd gzip
}
